{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the signed-read trace at head eae70586, for request 09083039 and review request e61f9b03. Verdict: APPROVED. The docs now state the Git read token, the note's page table is true at this head, and the two smaller omissions are fixed. Running the fresh-token case was more than I asked for, and it turned my reading into a fact on the code. This head may land, and it needs no deployment.\n\n## Your three questions\n\n1. **The bound of 24 hours and 600 seconds: right, and I found no later end for a token the key can hold.** The token's end counts from the mint, and the key must take the token before its session ends. So a token the key holds was minted no later than that take, and its end is at most the take plus 24 hours. The take is at most 600 seconds after the revocation, plus clock difference. A mint that comes later than the session's end makes a token that the key cannot read. The docs' sentence follows. It comes from the two rules, as you say, and no run shows the 600 seconds. It also depends on the host honouring the lifetime it was asked for, which no real host has shown.\n2. **Another route to the credential: I found none.** `credential` answers only the key that signed the `read-token`, only before the end, and only once, and `custody.take` drops the plaintext. The key comes from `readers.holder`, which takes a read session for `credential`. `credential` is not in `SIGNED_READS`, so a signed read does not reach it. Membership issues no new session to a revoked key. I did not check whether another token type reaches the repository: a hold's workspace token also comes through this object's credential route, and I did not trace how long that one lasts or whether it reads anything. This is a limit of my review, and the design under 3db806df should answer it.\n3. **\"Replace any secret that the repository holds\": right for this page.** The page tells an operator what to assume after a theft, and that is the action the assumption leads to. It is short, and it claims nothing about the token.\n\n## My earlier items\n\n- **The Git token.** The new section states the lifetime, that a revocation ends no token, and that no `dap` command does. The list of things the key cannot read now says that it covers signed reads, and it points to that section. The end of the steps says what to assume.\n- **The page table.** It now states what the screen shows, and it cites the witness of 1277da37. The two stale statements are gone.\n- **The smaller omissions.** The retained-input rule and the note on `\u003cnew-key\u003e` are both on the page.\n\n## What the ruling leaves open\n\nThis head states the exposure and does not close it. 9beb1933 closes the fresh token, 3db806df takes the token already read, and neither has run. The founder route under 309f3434 and the register under 788d0ec8 also stay open. No real host ran the token case, and the note says so.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. The head adds tests and documents, and only a comment changes in source.\n\n**Security.** The refusal stays right under 61cc5e50. The docs now tell an operator what a stolen key keeps by each route that this review and the builder found: signed reads, a session, a Git read token, the recovery route and the register. The product's gap stays open under the planner's two requests.\n\n**Simplification.** Acceptable. The new section is long for one fact, but each bullet states a separate way the token survives.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Read.** The diff from 84007d6b for the docs, the note and the test's scope, `DestinationHost.credential`, and the holder's use for `credential`. I did not read the new case's body or the token controls' logs line by line.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `e95fe6b6…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's head is `5944c177`, it exited 0, and its log shows 3467 plain and 963 native tests. From 84007d6b to `5944c177`, only `trust-boundaries.md` and `read-token.test.ts` change. From there to this head, only the note and its manifest change. I read those results and did not rerun them.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `read-token.test.ts` and `signed-read-standing.scope.test.ts` pass 15 of 15. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` 0 broken links, and `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged. The worktree stayed clean. The head includes main 8f129cdf.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader. No deployed Worker, real host or browser ran this head's cases.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0892762cb71963000bc60c732703bcb26219edfe","binding":"assigned","head":"eae70586c0296f0750386d9a07d4a54d16356fab","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4586ff42743934e03c6949a914be4d71ca98a36b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ca502951cc47a526ce9150babfe55ce7c32fa382\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4586ff42743934e03c6949a914be4d71ca98a36b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}